1871-@e9 [checkbox] checked                   # Checked checkbox
1872-@e10 [radio] selected                    # Selected radio
1873-```
1874-
1875:## Iframes
1876-
1877:Snapshots automatically detect and inline iframe content. When the main-frame snapshot runs, each `Iframe` node is resolved and its child accessibility tree is included directly beneath it in the output. Refs assigned to elements inside iframes carry frame context, so interactions like `click`, `fill`, and `type` work without manually switching frames.
1878-
1879-```bash
1880-agent-browser snapshot -i
1881-# @e1 [heading] "Checkout"
1882:# @e2 [Iframe] "payment-frame"
1883-#   @e3 [input] "Card number"
1884-#   @e4 [input] "Expiry"
1885-#   @e5 [button] "Pay"
1886-# @e6 [button] "Cancel"
1887-
1888:# Interact with iframe elements directly using their refs
1889-agent-browser fill @e3 "4111111111111111"
1890-agent-browser fill @e4 "12/28"
1891-agent-browser click @e5
1892-```
1893-
1894-**Key details:**
1895:- Only one level of iframe nesting is expanded (iframes within iframes are not recursed)
1896:- Cross-origin iframes that block accessibility tree access are silently skipped
1897:- Empty iframes or iframes with no interactive content are omitted from the output
1898:- To scope a snapshot to a single iframe, use `frame @ref` then `snapshot -i`
